rustc_codegen_js: host-delegated slice::sort, str case mapping, and charCodeAt str cursors.

1. `core::slice::sort::{stable,unstable}::sort`: replace `#[inline(always)]` with
   `#[inline(never)]` + `rcgjs_slice_{stable,unstable}_sort` diagnostic items and a
   tiny insertion-sort fallback calling `rcgjs_sort_cmp` so driftsort/ipnsort and
   the 4 KiB stack scratch buffer never reach MIR, while `jsc-link` lowers both
   entry points directly to `__rt.slice_sort` (spec-stable ES2018 index merge sort).
2. `alloc::str::{to_lowercase,to_uppercase}`: tag with `rcgjs_str_to_{lowercase,uppercase}`
   and delegate to `__rt.host_str_to_{lowercase,uppercase}` (native String regions
   lower directly to `str_to_{lowercase,uppercase}` / `bstr_to_{lowercase,uppercase}`),
   eliminating `core::unicode::unicode_data::conversions` tables.
3. `core::str::iter::{Chars,Bytes}`: replace `slice::Iter<u8>` backing with
   `{ s: &str, start: usize, end: usize }` cursors reading bytes via
   `rcgjs_str_byte_at` (`s.charCodeAt(i)` under `js-str=bytes`) and slicing via
   `rcgjs_str_slice_unchecked` (`s.slice(start, end)` under `js-str=bytes`).

